ian-empire","cpn":"Sasanian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Persian_Wars","c":3},{"y":252,"t":"vassal_end","x":"252: Armenia is lost.","cp":"kingdom-of-armenia","cpn":"Kingdom of Armenia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Persian_Wars","c":2},{"y":253,"t":"contest_start","x":"253: Shapur I storms into Syria.","cp":"sasanian-empire","cpn":"Sasanian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Persian_Wars","c":3},{"y":260,"t":"contest_end","x":"260: Valerian is captured.","cp":"sasanian-empire","cpn":"Sasanian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Persian_Wars","c":2},{"y":260,"t":"loss","x":"260: the Agri Decumates are given up.","cp":"Alemanni","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agri_Decumates","c":3},{"y":260,"t":"loss","x":"260: the Gallic Empire.","cp":"gallic-empire","cpn":"Gallic Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crisis_of_the_Third_Century","c":3},{"y":267,"t":"loss","x":"267: the Palmyrene Empire.","cp":"palmyrene-empire","cpn":"Palmyrene Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crisis_of_the_Third_Century","c":2},{"y":271,"t":"loss","x":"271: Dacia is abandoned.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Dacia","c":3},{"y":271,"t":"loss","x":"late 271: Zenobia takes Egypt.","cp":"palmyrene-empire","cpn":"Palmyrene Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crisis_of_the_Third_Century","c":3},{"y":272,"t":"gain","x":"272: Rome restores the East.","cp":"palmyrene-empire","cpn":"Palmyrene Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palmyrene_Empire","c":2},{"y":274,"t":"gain","x":"274: Aurelian reunites the empire.","cp":"gallic-empire","cpn":"Gallic Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crisis_of_the_Third_Century","c":3},{"y":277,"t":"gain","x":"277: Probus retakes the Agri Decumates.","cp":"Alemanni","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agri_Decumates","c":2},{"y":284,"t":"rename","x":"284: Diocletian takes the throne (20 November 284) and reorders the empire; 'Diocletian reorganised and restored much of it in 285'.","m":11,"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Roman_emperors","c":3},{"y":286,"t":"loss","x":"286: Carausius holds Britain.","cp":"Britannic Empire (Carausius and Allectus)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Britain","c":3},{"y":296,"t":"contest_start","x":"296: Narseh's war.","cp":"sasanian-empire","cpn":"Sasanian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Persian_Wars","c":2},{"y":296,"t":"gain","x":"296: Britain returns.","cp":"Britannic Empire (Carausius and Allectus)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Britain","c":3},{"y":298,"t":"loss","x":"298: Rome leaves the Dodekaschoinos.","cp":"kingdom-of-kush","cpn":"Kingdom of Kush","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yesebokheamani","c":2},{"y":299,"t":"contest_end","x":"299: the Peace of Nisibis.","cp":"sasanian-empire","cpn":"Sasanian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Persian_Wars","c":3},{"y":299,"t":"gain","x":"299: Rome gains the land beyond the Tigris.","cp":"sasanian-empire","cpn":"Sasanian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Persian_Wars","c":3},{"y":299,"t":"vassal_start","x":"299: Armenia is in Roman hands.","cp":"kingdom-of-armenia","cpn":"Kingdom of Armenia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Persian_Wars","c":2},{"y":300,"t":"loss","x":"about 300: the Agri Decumates are given up for good.","cp":"Alemanni","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agri_Decumates","c":1},{"y":306,"t":"rename","x":"306: Constantine is acclaimed.","m":7,"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Roman_emperors","c":3},{"y":330,"t":"capital_move","x":"330: Constantine moves the capital to Constantinople.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Empire","c":3},{"y":358,"t":"loss","x":"358: the Rhine delta goes to the Salian Franks.","cp":"salian-franks","cpn":"Salian Franks","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germanic_Wars","c":2},{"y":359,"t":"contest_start","x":"359: Shapur II takes Amida.","cp":"sasanian-empire","cpn":"Sasanian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Persian_Wars","c":3},{"y":363,"t":"contest_end","x":"363: Julian dies; Jovian makes peace.","cp":"sasanian-empire","cpn":"Sasanian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Persian_Wars","c":2},{"y":363,"t":"loss","x":"363: the settlement of 299 is undone.","cp":"sasanian-empire","cpn":"Sasanian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Persian_Wars","c":2},{"y":363,"t":"vassal_end","x":"363: Armenia is abandoned.","cp":"kingdom-of-armenia","cpn":"Kingdom of Armenia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Persian_Wars","c":2},{"y":367,"t":"contest_start","x":"367: the Great Conspiracy.","cp":"Picts, Saxons, Scoti and Attacotti","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Britain","c":3},{"y":371,"t":"contest_end","x":"371: Britain is whole again.","cp":"Picts, Saxons, Scoti and Attacotti","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Britain","c":1},{"y":378,"t":"contest_start","x":"August 378: the Goths at Adrianople.","m":8,"cp":"gothia","cpn":"Gothia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodosius_I","c":2},{"y":379,"t":"rename","x":"379: Theodosius I is made emperor in the East at Sirmium, 'formally invested with the purple... on 19 January 379'.","m":1,"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Roman_emperors","c":3},{"y":382,"t":"contest_end","x":"3 October 382: the Gothic treaty.","m":10,"cp":"gothia","cpn":"Gothia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodosius_I","c":3},{"y":383,"t":"loss","x":"383: Magnus Maximus is acclaimed in Britain.","cp":"Magnus Maximus (usurper)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodosius_I","c":3},{"y":383,"t":"loss","x":"25 August 383: Gratian is killed at Lugdunum.","m":8,"cp":"Magnus Maximus (usurper)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodosius_I","c":2},{"y":387,"t":"loss","x":"387: Maximus takes Italy.","cp":"Magnus Maximus (usurper)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodosius_I","c":2},{"y":387,"t":"vassal_start","x":"387: Armenia is divided.","cp":"kingdom-of-armenia","cpn":"Kingdom of Armenia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Persian_Wars","c":2},{"y":388,"t":"gain","x":"summer 388: Theodosius defeats Maximus.","cp":"Magnus Maximus (usurper)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodosius_I","c":3},{"y":388,"t":"gain","x":"388: Britain and Gaul come back.","cp":"Magnus Maximus (usurper)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodosius_I","c":2},{"y":392,"t":"contest_start","x":"22 August 392: Eugenius is proclaimed.","m":8,"cp":"Eugenius (usurper)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodosius_I","c":2},{"y":394,"t":"contest_end","x":"6 September 394: the Frigidus.","m":9,"cp":"Eugenius (usurper)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodosius_I","c":3},{"y":395,"t":"split","x":"17 January 395: the West.","m":1,"cp":"western-roman-empire","cpn":"Western Roman Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodosius_I","c":3},{"y":395,"t":"split","x":"17 January 395: the East.","m":1,"cp":"eastern-roman-empire","cpn":"Eastern Roman Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodosius_I","c":3},{"y":395,"t":"dissolve","x":"395: the undivided Roman Empire ends.","m":1,"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodosius_I","c":3}],"wars":[{"name":"Aelius Gallus's expedition to Arabia Felix","from":-25,"to":-24,"outcome":"Failure: 'a complete failure', disease 'destroyed the greater part of the army' and 'the Arabs drove the Romans from territory they had held'; Gallus retreated in sixty days and was succeeded as prefect by Petronius.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aelius_Gallus"},{"name":"Roman-Kushite war","from":-23,"to":-22,"outcome":"Rome won on the field: the governor 'pillaged northern Nubia and sacked Napata (22 BC) before returning home'; 'the peace treaty signed in 22 BC between Rome and Meroe under Augustus and Amanirenas' left the Roman Egyptian border 'extended to Hiera Sykaminos…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mero%C3%AB"},{"name":"Augustus's German campaigns","from":-12,"to":9,"outcome":"Drusus's invasions up the Elbe (12-9 BC), Tiberius reaching the Elbe (1-4), then Teutoburg: '9 AD: Roman Empire is forced to strategically withdraw from Germania'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germanic_Wars"},{"name":"Great Illyrian Revolt","from":6,"to":9,"outcome":"'6-9: Uprising in Illyricum' (Germanic Wars page); the interior is Roman again in Cliopatria's 9 shape.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germanic_Wars"},{"name":"Germanicus's campaigns east of the Rhine","from":14,"to":17,"outcome":"'14-16: Roman retaliation against Cherusci, Chatti, Bructeri and Marsi'; '17: Cessation of military offensives east of the Rhine'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germanic_Wars"},{"name":"Aedemon's revolt in Mauretania","from":40,"to":44,"outcome":"Rome won: after Aedemon's death in 42 'Sabalus surrendered in 44 AD, leading to the annexation of western Mauretania', and 'Around 44 AD, the region was annexed to Rome and divided into two provinces' (Mauretania page).","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mauretania"},{"name":"Roman conquest of Britain","from":43,"to":87,"outcome":"Claudius's invasion of 43, the Fosse Way line by 47, the Ordovices conquered in 78, Agricola in Scotland 77-84 and the decision of 87 to abandon most of the land north of the Cheviot Hills.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Britain"},{"name":"Boudican revolt","from":60,"to":61,"outcome":"Rome crushed the allied tribes: Suetonius's army 'decisively defeated the allied tribes in a final battle' (site unknown); the defeat 'consolidated Roman rule in southern Britain' and 'the occupation of Britain continued' (Boudican revolt page).","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boudican_revolt"},{"name":"Roman-Parthian war over Armenia (Corbulo)","from":58,"to":63,"outcome":"Corbulo overthrew Tiridates in the 58 crisis; the war ended in 63 with the Peace of Rhandeia: Tiridates and his descendants rule Armenia on condition that the Roman emperor confers the kingship.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Parthian_Wars"},{"name":"First Jewish–Roman War","from":66,"to":73,"outcome":"Rome won: Jerusalem 'fell in the summer of 70' and the war ended with 'the fall of Masada in 73/74'; Judaea 'later became a directly ruled province' and Legio X Fretensis stayed to suppress the last pockets (First Jewish-Roman War page).","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Jewish%E2%80%93Roman_War"},{"name":"Domitian's Chatti war","from":82,"to":83,"outcome":"'Roman armies conquer the territory of Chatti with the help of Mattiaci, Hermunduri and Cherusci'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germanic_Wars"},{"name":"Trajan's Dacian Wars","from":101,"to":106,"outcome":"Peace in 102 after the first war ('a series of engagements'), conquest in 105-106; Dacia an imperial province on 11 August 106.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Dacia"},{"name":"Trajan's Parthian war","from":113,"to":117,"outcome":"Armenia annexed 114, northern Mesopotamia 115, Ctesiphon taken 115; 'revolts erupted' and Hadrian reversed the policy, 'surrendering the territories of Armenia, Mesopotamia, and Adiabene back to their previous rulers'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Parthian_Wars"},{"name":"Bar Kokhba revolt","from":132,"to":135,"outcome":"Rome won: Betar, the rebels' main stronghold, was captured and destroyed in 135 and Simon bar Kokhba was killed; the revolt 'likely ended in early 136' (Eck).","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bar_Kokhba_revolt"},{"name":"Parthian war of Lucius Verus","from":161,"to":165,"outcome":"Vologases IV took Edessa and ravaged Syria (161), Statius Priscus crowned an Armenian king (163), Avidius Cassius invaded Mesopotamia (164) and sacked Ctesiphon (165); an epidemic forced withdrawal.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Parthian_Wars"},{"name":"Marcomannic Wars","from":166,"to":180,"outcome":"Roman victory with no territorial change: the infobox of the Marcomannic Wars page gives 'Status quo ante bellum' and says the Roman plans to annex Sarmatia (Hungarian Plain) and Marcomannia were abandoned; no ground changed hands.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marcomannic_Wars"},{"name":"Severus's Parthian war","from":195,"to":198,"outcome":"Invasion of Mesopotamia 195, Ctesiphon sacked again 197; 'the Roman acquisition of northern Mesopotamia, as far as the areas around Nisibis and Singara'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Parthian_Wars"},{"name":"Severus's Caledonian campaign","from":208,"to":210,"outcome":"Severus 'moved north in 208 or 209' and 'By 210 ... had returned to York'; no lasting border change.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Britain"},{"name":"Parthian war of Caracalla and Macrinus","from":216,"to":217,"outcome":"Caracalla 'sacked Arbela in 216'; Macrinus 'lost a battle against the Parthians at Nisibis' and 'was forced to pay tribute to Parthia'; the last of the Parthian Wars.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Parthian_Wars"},{"name":"Persian invasions of Ardashir I and Shapur I","from":230,"to":260,"outcome":"Raids from 230, Carrhae, Nisibis and Hatra taken in 238-240 and retaken in 243, Misiche and peace in 244, Armenia lost in the early 250s, Barbalissos and probably Antioch in 253, Valerian captured 258-260.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Persian_Wars"},{"name":"Alemannic and Frankish wars","from":259,"to":370,"outcome":"Retreat behind the Rhine 259-260, Probus 277-278, Constantius's Franks 292, Constantine across the Rhine 308 and 310, Julian 355-360, Valentinian 368-370 (Germanic Wars page).","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germanic_Wars"},{"name":"Breakaway of the Gallic and Palmyrene Empires","from":260,"to":274,"outcome":"Gaul, Britain and Hispania broke off in 260; the Palmyrene Empire took Syria, Palestine and Egypt (267, Egypt late 271); 'By late 274, the Roman Empire had been reunited'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crisis_of_the_Third_Century"},{"name":"Carus's Persian war","from":283,"to":283,"outcome":"'In 283 the emperor Carus launched a successful invasion of Persia, sacking its capital, Ctesiphon'; Carus died before finishing it; no border change.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Persian_Wars"},{"name":"Carausian revolt","from":286,"to":296,"outcome":"The 'short-lived Britannic Empire from 286 to 296'; Constantius Chlorus launched a second offensive in 293.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Britain"},{"name":"Narseh's war","from":296,"to":299,"outcome":"Galerius beaten near Carrhae in 296 or 297, victor in 298 ('sacked the capital Ctesiphon'); the Peace of Nisibis gave the Romans 'control of the area between the Tigris and the Greater Zab'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Persian_Wars"},{"name":"Shapur II's wars","from":335,"to":363,"outcome":"From the mid-330s Shapur II won at Singara (348), took Amida (359) and Bezabde and Singara (360); Julian died at Samarra and Jovian 'surrendered their former possessions east of the Tigris, as well as Nisibis and Singara' (363).","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Persian_Wars"},{"name":"Great Conspiracy","from":367,"to":367,"outcome":"'in 367, a general assault of Saxons, Picts, Scoti and Attacotti' (Roman Britain page); the page gives no outcome.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Britain"},{"name":"Gothic War as far as the treaty of 382","from":378,"to":382,"outcome":"Valens killed at Adrianople in August 378; the treaty of 3 October 382 let the Goths 'settle some tracts of Roman land south of the Danube'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodosius_I"},{"name":"Usurpation of Magnus Maximus","from":383,"to":388,"outcome":"Acclaimed in Britain in 383, Gratian killed at Lugdunum on 25 August 383, the peace broken in 387, Maximus defeated at Poetovio in 388 and executed on 28 August 388.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodosius_I"},{"name":"Eugenius and the Battle of the Frigidus","from":392,"to":394,"outcome":"Eugenius proclaimed at Lugdunum on 22 August 392; Theodosius defeated him at the Frigidus on 6 September 394 and ruled both halves until 17 January 395.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodosius_I"}],"certainty":[{"from":-27,"to":8,"level":"soft","note":"The Augustan conquests are not yet fixed: Germania to the Elbe, the Alps, Arabia Felix and the client kingdoms are approximate (no survey or treaty on the pages opened)."},{"from":9,"to":259,"level":"sharp","note":"The Rhine, Danube, Hadrian's and the Antonine Walls and the Euphrates are fixed frontier lines; the eastern desert edge, the Mesopotamian cities, Dacia's northern edge and the client kingdoms stay soft."},{"from":260,"to":298,"level":"soft","note":"Gaul and the East are in the breakaway empires and the Rhine-Danube line is moving; every border is approximate."},{"from":299,"to":395,"level":"sharp","note":"The Peace of Nisibis (299) and the partition of Armenia (384/387) are treaty lines; the Gothic settlement south of the Danube (382) and Britain stay soft."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Empire","title":"Roman Empire"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Roman_provinces","title":"List of Roman provinces"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Augustus","title":"Augustus"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_client_kingdoms","title":"Roman client kingdoms"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Britain","title":"Roman Britain"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Dacia","title":"Roman Dacia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crisis_of_the_Third_Century","title":"Crisis of the Third Century"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Parthian_Wars","title":"Roman-Parthian Wars"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Persian_Wars","title":"Roman-Persian Wars"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agri_Decumates","title":"Agri Decumates"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germanic_Wars","title":"Germanic Wars (Roman-Germanic wars)"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodosius_I","title":"Theodosius I"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aelius_Gallus","title":"Aelius Gallus"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Roman_emperors","title":"List of Roman emperors"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polemon_II_of_Pontus","title":"Polemon II of Pontus"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiberius_Julius_Cotys_I","title":"Tiberius Julius Cotys I"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mero%C3%AB","title":"Meroe"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Kush","title":"Kingdom of Kush"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yesebokheamani","title":"Yesebokheamani"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mauretania","title":"Mauretania"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palmyrene_Empire","title":"Palmyrene Empire"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Jewish%E2%80%93Roman_War","title":"First Jewish–Roman War"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bar_Kokhba_revolt","title":"Bar Kokhba revolt"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boudican_revolt","title":"Boudican revolt"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marcomannic_Wars","title":"Marcomannic Wars"}]}